re  I love hearing all of this like stuff  you don't see on TV I find it so  fascinating as a Survivor fan  right yeah um let's Circle back to the  immunity challenge okay yeah we'll do  the immunity Challenge and then we'll  talk a little bit about reward but  immunity like when you notice that you  know these two tribes are working kind  of like helping each other because they  pretty much want to send you guys to  Tribal Council you guys hired the full  six like you have a full tribe like is  that stressful watching it and seeing it  all unfold  so uh I didn't realize it until Jeff  told us after the challenge was over  um looking back and watching the episode  James saw it happening  um in Cassidy and Geo saw it happening  too but  when it comes like I don't think anybody  realized this I hate losing like it is a  toxic creative mind like I despise it  and so I get so competitive in that  moment I was also incredibly frustrated  that I wasn't able to do the puzzle  myself  um so I just wanted to make sure that I  was helping and supporting Carla and  Ryan do the puzzle  um what you guys don't see is there was  a moment where  um  we thought we had solved the puzzle  correctly and so we're all celebrating  and streaming and high-fiving and  hugging each other and just like no  that's not it oh my gosh and so we go  into panic mode and have to go back into  the puzzle and at that moment that's  when they start helping each other  um another thing that you guys don't see  is in the challenge beforehand when they  had to choose who was going to go on the  journey  um it was the journey with James and  Noel  um Dwight asked Baca to send Noel  and so when Dwight when Noel were  helping Baca solve that puzzle that was  their way of saying hey you had our  backs last time like we're gonna do you  a solid and and pay you back for that  favor and that's why Dwight and Noel  ended up helping Baca oh wow I love this  tea I love this sorority I love hearing  all this stuff yeah um and then quickly  going to the reward Challenge and then  you know you have Cody come to your camp  like obviously it's kind of  unprecedented like you don't know what's  gonna happen and he's kind of bartering  and seeing what he can get out of you  guys did you guys have a strategy if  they were going to come to your camp and  then when he did like what happened was  it just chaos  it wasn't necessarily chaos Cody's  mentality  um and I think he stayed  um pretty loyal to like this mentality  of um I'm just here to have fun and you  know just like a surfer bro from Hawaii  and Dwight's calling the shots at our  camp and he's The Mastermind and I'm  just listening to what he's telling me  to do  um My Tribe told me to take your machete  they want to you know cut you guys off  but hey I'm just a peacemaker and I'm  not trying to piss anybody off and and  tell you what why don't I just do you  guys a solid my tribe is going to be  super mad at me when I get back but like  why don't I just take your fishing gear  and I'll be the first to admit like I am  a terrible negotiator like I am horrible  at it right  um I'm good at a lot of things but it is  not that so um I was just like here take  everything whatever you want as long as  you don't take my machete I didn't  realize  um some of our tribe mates were a little  annoyed by uh what Cody was able to get  away with but  um after seeing them working together  and knowing that they were coming for us  I was just so grateful that they didn't  take the things that we needed most  absolutely now just to kind of wrap up  your journey on Survivor seeing it all  unfold on Wednesday night how are you  feeling now and is this Survivor Journey  everything that you hoped it would be  it absolutely is not everything that I  hoped it would be I've got so much more  gain left in me I I felt like  um it ended way too soon but of course  I'm gonna say that like I I obviously  have like this Survivor bucket list of  all these things that I wanted to  accomplish  but I'm the type of person that believes  that like everything happens for a  reason right so if everything happens  for a reason then like I have to believe  that this happened for a reason as well  and maybe I don't understand what it is  exactly like just yet I will at some  point and and I'm trying to be open to  that  um but I'm sad my journey was was cut  too soon I my nine days out there I got  everything out of that game that I  wanted to  um in terms of  um surviving and and living off the  island and and proving to myself I  didn't have anything to prove to anybody  else like  in my everyday life like you know I'm a  nurse I'm a great mom I'm a great friend  like I I I just took care of covet  patients for a couple of years like I  didn't need to be to go out there to  learn like how tough and strong I was  what I wanted was to be able to have the  experience like I said in my in my  pre-game interview I was so scared of  just never being able to play so to go  out there and have the time of my life  and not have to go to tribal for nine  days and and not be paranoid and and  worried just to go out there and have a  blast was just the greatest gift in the  world and I'm so grateful for it well  that's a great outlook on everything  despite it not necessarily playing out  the way you wanted but I would be  totally down for you to come on the show  again I loved watching you so I feel  like we need to get another season of  people who were voted off before jury  that you know make it happen but it was  lovely chatting with you  um I'm so sorry and the way it did but  again I loved watching you so thank you  so much I appreciate it thank you so so  much for your love and support
 

